\uc0\u9474  \u55357 \u56522  REPRODUCTIVE NEUROENDOCRINOLOGY                                         \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474                                                                              \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  Researchers utilize kisspeptin-10 to investigate how the brain controls    \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  reproductive hormone release. The peptide stimulates GnRH neuron activity, \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  triggering cascades that regulate luteinizing hormone (LH), follicle-      \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  stimulating hormone (FSH), and testosterone production.                    \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474                                                                              \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  Essential Research Areas:                                                  \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \'95 Puberty mechanisms and development                                       \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \'95 Fertility regulation and reproductive aging                              \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \'95 Hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal (HPG) axis function                     \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \'95 Sex differences in reproductive control                                  \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \'95 Metabolic influences on reproduction                                     \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474                                                                              \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  \u55357 \u56620  ONCOLOGY & DIAGNOSTIC DEVELOPMENT                                      \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474                                                                              \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  Recent research explores kisspeptin-10's potential in cancer diagnostics   \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  and tumor biology. When labeled with radioactive compounds, the peptide    \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  shows promise as a diagnostic imaging agent. Additionally, studies         \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  demonstrate that kisspeptin suppresses cancer cell migration through       \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474  multiple signaling pathways.                                               \u9474 \
\uc0\u9474                                                                              \u9474 \
